://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7872b3bab6a63a0215c519f8dd2eaeeb4c84043c.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued September 14 at 4:05PM MDT until September 14 at 7:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nWest Central Archuleta County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* Until 700 PM MDT.\n\n* At 405 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBayfield, Ignacio, Oxford, Falfa, Bondad, Chimney Rock and\nLonetree.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nSquaw Creek, Florida River, Rock Creek, Cat Creek, Freeman Creek,\nDry Creek, Hayden Creek, Sheep Creek, Devil Creek, Yellowjacket\nCreek, Dudley Creek, Elk Creek, Spring Creek, Piedra River, Pinos\nRiver, Los, Stollsteimer Creek, Indian Creek, Animas River, Ute\nCreek, Heflin Creek, Ignacio Creek, San Juan River, West Fork Devil\nCreek, Salt Creek, Crowbar Creek, Archuleta Creek, Round Meadow\nCreek and Beaver Creek.","ends":"2026-09-14T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2ffe8352e62cd3127e8b853359e3ac057c4ee87c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.2ffe8352e62cd3127e8b853359e3ac057c4ee87c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-14T18:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 141850 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1250 PM MDT Mon Sep 14 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - There is a chance for strong storms over the next few days, capable of producing hail, gusty winds, and heavy rainfall. - Moderate to heavy rainfall could lead to localized flash flooding, rockfalls, and mudslides at times this week. - Temperatures return","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-14T18:55:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Critical fire weather conditions are not expected to develop this week, as relative humidities remain elevated thanks to ample moisture across the region. Wetting rains remain in the forecast, with some flash flooding risk each day on flood prone burn scars and within flashy drainages. Lightning from thunderstorms will remain a threat to crews as well. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"pgs01","station_name":"Pagosa Springs","distance_km":2.6,"soil_temp_5cm_f":69.33,"soil_temp_15cm_f":63.79,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":2.12,"wind_speed_mph":6.59,"air_temp_f":63.16,"relative_humidity":0.705,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/pgs01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KPSO","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KPSO 142235Z AUTO VRB03KT 6SM -TSRA HZ FEW011 BKN033 OVC047 15/12 A3024 RMK AO2 LTG DSNT ALQDS","temp_f":59,"wind_dir":"VRB","wind_kt":3,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":6,"cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1024.1,"observed":1789425300,"raw_taf":null,"url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KPSO&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":41,"category":"Good","parameter":"O3","reporting_area":"Southern Ute Indian Reservation","observed":"2026-09-14 15","by_parameter":{"O3":{"aqi":41,"category":"Good","reporting_area":"Southern Ute Indian Reservation","observed":"2026-09-14 15"},"PM2.5"